def car_race_collision(n: int):
    """
    Imagine a straight, infinitely long road.
    n cars are driving left to right; simultaneously, another n cars drive right to left. 
    The two sets of cars start very far from each other. All cars move at the same speed.
    A collision occurs when a car moving left to right hits one moving right to left.
    Despite collisions, cars continue on their paths unchanged.

    This function outputs the number of such collisions.
    """
    return n * (n - 1) // 2
